Wen,

I have not yet fully penetrated Zaidi et al.’s paper but did look at the appendix to try to understand the reasons for their analysis.  It seems they wish to shear projections such that there is a positiveness or negativeness along an axis that separates male and female means, which would highlight hypermasculine or hyperfeminine traits (landmark displacements).  I tend to agree with you, because in this way, maintaining Euclidean geometry is not necessarily important.

However, using the arithmetic mean for an overall score is a method that currently eludes me as appropriate.  I agree that I would rely on Gunz’s measure for an overall score.

Cheers!
Mike

