This might seem like an obvious question but here it goes. I want to compare the relative fit of different of models of trait evolution for each subclade in my phylogeny. To reduce the dimensionality of my high dimensional dataset before model fitting, I am wondering if it makes more sense to do a PCA for all the species in my tree and subset the resulting PC scores by subclade or do a PCA on each subclade prior to model fitting. I plan to use PC scores for model fitting.

