Hello everybody,

I am hoping you can help me figure out the following: after having used the integration.test function, I would like to know the % each PLS captures of the total covariance but I am kinda stumped on what might be a good way how to go about it in R!

I was initially thinking along the lines of generating the covariance matrix of the two block (e.g. cov.il.is <http://cov.il.is> <-cov(il.is.int <http://il.is.int>$A1.matrix,il.is.int <http://il.is.int>$A2.matrix) and computing the eigenvalue for each PLS , and then regress these. But of course the cov matrix has a very different structure, so that will not work. I am clearly thinking in the wrong direction, but for now I can’t seem to see the tree in the forrest. Any ideas?

Best wishes,
Katrien

